      {
        "id": "read_file",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Read a text file from the project by its path, relative to the project root. Returns the file content as plain text.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241702,
        "_key": "read_file"
      },
      {
        "id": "run_command",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Execute a NEXUS cockpit command. Commands follow cockpit's real interaction contract (v1.0.0). Available commands:\nforge pipeline list — List all pipelines\nforge pipeline create <name> — Create a new pipeline\nforge pipeline run <id> — Trigger a pipeline run\nforge pipeline add-node <pipeline_id> <type> — Add a node to a pipeline\nforge pipeline connect <pipeline_id> <from_id> <to_id> — Connect two nodes with an optional condition\nforge pipeline arm <id> — Enable pipeline scheduler\nforge pipeline disarm <id> — Disable pipeline scheduler\nforge pipeline delete <id> — Delete a pipeline\nforge pipeline export <id> — Export pipeline as JSON\nforge pipeline import <json> — Import pipeline from JSON\nforge seam compile <source> — Compile SEAM source → constraint field + JS\nforge seam validate <source> — Validate SEAM source (Pass 0 only)\nforge seam chunk <source> — Chunk SEAM/spec source into delivery protocol chunks\nforge idea list — List ideas from Idearium\nforge idea create <title> — Create a new idea in Idearium\nforge gap list — List gaps\nforge gap create <title> — Create a gap\nforge gap resolve <id> <resolution> — Resolve a gap\nforge snapshot create — Create Idearium snapshot\nforge trust list — List all trust scores (Beta distribution)\nforge trust record <sourceId> — Record a trust event for a source\nforge guardian dispatch <provider> <prompt> — Dispatch prompt to Guardian agent\nforge guardian health — Check Guardian connection\nforge idearium health — Check Idearium connection\nforge bus emit <channel> — Emit a SISO bus event\nforge bus history — Show recent SISO bus events\nforge jaa stats — Show JAA store row counts by table\nforge jaa query <table> — Query a JAA table\nforge help — Show all available commands\nAlso: \"forge help\" lists commands.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241711,
        "_key": "run_command"
      },
      {
        "id": "diagnose",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Diagnose the NEXUS system via the real diagnostic service. Actions: \"status\" (every system's online/friction/sigma/open-gap state), \"gaps\" (open gaps, optionally filtered by system), \"friction\" (current friction readings), \"summary\" (deep diagnosis of ONE system — requires system name, e.g. guardian/cortex/ollama/idearium/bridge), \"tension\" (cross-system relational tension), \"heal\" (trigger the diagnostic self-heal surface).",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241711,
        "_key": "diagnose"
      },
      {
        "id": "move_data",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Move data in/out of Cortex (NEXUS's memory). Actions: \"push\" (store content with tags into a memory tier: recent/session/long), \"recall\" (retrieve memories by intent/query), \"read\" (tail the last N rows of a named table, e.g. chat_log, event_log, gaps), \"insert\" (write a raw row into a named table). There is deliberately no delete — nothing is lost, ever.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241712,
        "_key": "move_data"
      },
      {
        "id": "run_pipeline",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Run the NEXUS autonomous execution pipeline (build → sandbox-verify → compare-to-golden → governed promote). Actions: \"run\" (start a pipeline from a spec — requires specPath; optional outputDir, provider, testCommand), \"status\" (get one pipeline by id — requires id), \"list\" (recent pipeline runs). The pipeline self-gates: unproven output is never promoted.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241714,
        "_key": "run_pipeline"
      },
      {
        "id": "nexus_intelligence",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Query NEXUS's live intelligence and event surfaces directly, one real signal at a time — use this instead of a full diagnose \"summary\" when you only need one answer, not a whole system report. Actions: \"events\" (event ledger — optional system filter), \"status\" (intelligence system health snapshot), \"patterns\" (crystallized execution-outcome log — domain/verb/outcome triples), \"causalPatterns\" (recurring CAUSAL event-sequence detection over the live causal graph — different from \"patterns\"; requires enough recent event_log activity, degrades to patternsFound:0 honestly when there isn't), \"rca\" (root cause analysis entries), \"intuition\" (fast intuition answer — requires prompt), \"mastermind\" (causal analysis — requires prompt; reaches RFR2's causal toolkit internally), \"cfr\" (current CFR field: coherence/friction/entropy/regime), \"lattice\" (associative/causal graph neighbors for a subject — requires system), \"stream\" (live SSE liveness probe on a named system — requires system).",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241714,
        "_key": "nexus_intelligence"
      },
      {
        "id": "run_closed_loop",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Import a spec and automatically build a repository from it: create the spec manifest, chunk it, and populate every chunk via the WARP build spine, then create a repo. Params: name (required unless repoUuid given), description (the spec intent), type (component|service|library, default component), agent (ollama default), repoUuid (optional — build INTO an existing repo, e.g. one just created by the Import Project screen, instead of starting from an empty spec). Returns the spec id, populate progress, and repo id. Use run_pipeline afterward to build→verify→promote from the spec path.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241715,
        "_key": "run_closed_loop"
      },
      {
        "id": "module_builder",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Build a new NEXUS module from a natural-language description, running the full spec → QC → build pipeline. Returns the build result. Use when the user wants to CREATE a new component or capability.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241715,
        "_key": "module_builder"
      },
      {
        "id": "run_adversarial",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Run an adversarial critique pass over the current system stream — attacks recent activity to surface violations, weaknesses, and contradictions. Use to stress-test a proposal or check for problems.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241715,
        "_key": "run_adversarial"
      },
      {
        "id": "axiom_check",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Check a prompt, spec, or proposed action against the NEXUS axioms. Returns which axioms are engaged and any violations. Use before acting on something consequential.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241715,
        "_key": "axiom_check"
      },
      {
        "id": "analyze",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Deep analytical answer to a question about the system or a problem, using the analysis faculty (assembles context and reasons over it). Use for \"why\" and \"how\" questions that need reasoning, not just a lookup.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241715,
        "_key": "analyze"
      },
      {
        "id": "intuition",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Fast, associative, pattern-based answer from what the system already knows — cortex's own intuition faculty (<50ms, no model call). Falls through to null if there is no confident answer; use analyze for a deeper, reasoned answer.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241715,
        "_key": "intuition"
      },
      {
        "id": "mastermind",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Strategic, predictive, causal answer — cortex's own mastermind faculty, answering \"if this is true, what follows?\" using the real causal graph. The opposite question from intuition's \"what does this resemble?\".",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241715,
        "_key": "mastermind"
      },
      {
        "id": "synthesize",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Synthesize a real, structured build contract (fileName, primitives, compartmentUuid, synthesized context, endState, conditions, axioms, tools) from plain-text context — the same the_officiator hat and B1 schema officiate() uses for staged artifacts, but callable directly by any agent for its OWN reasoning. Does NOT queue a contract by default — pass submit:true to also submit one via the real RAID contract-intake path.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241716,
        "_key": "synthesize"
      },
      {
        "id": "call_system",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Call any registered NEXUS system. Give an `intent` (natural-language capability, resolved via the registry) OR an explicit `system` + `path`. Returns the system's response. Use to reach a capability you do not have a dedicated tool for.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241716,
        "_key": "call_system"
      },
      {
        "id": "ui_spotlight",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Guide the user's attention in the NEXUS UI. action \"on\" highlights a system (target: guardian/cortex/idearium/...); \"off\" clears it; \"step\" walks the user through a sequence of steps. Use to show the user WHERE something is happening while you assist.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241716,
        "_key": "ui_spotlight"
      },
      {
        "id": "ui_nerve",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Surface the live NEXUS \"nervous system\" field (the CFR sigma field) in the UI. action \"on\" shows it, \"off\" hides it, \"sigma\" pushes a specific field value. Use to make the system's live state visible to the user.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241716,
        "_key": "ui_nerve"
      },
      {
        "id": "query_recall",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Search past conversations and stored memory for relevant context. Use when the user references something from before (\"what did we decide about X\", \"the thing we discussed\") or when past context would help. Params: query (required — what to search for), intent (optional: general|session_resume|pattern_lookup|crystal_query|debug_failure|gap_fill|causal_trace, default general). Returns ranked past exchanges. Recall uses lexical (word-overlap), recency, failure-pattern, BEP-pattern, and causal-graph-connectivity ranking — 5 real lanes, weighted per intent.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241717,
        "_key": "query_recall"
      },
      {
        "id": "browser_action",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Control NEXUS' real browser (Clear Glass) — navigate to a URL, take a screenshot, show a real toast notification, read/mutate the DOM, manage cookies, or register a backend URL listener that fires a hook on matching traffic. This is a real browser, not a simulation; actions take real time and can fail for real reasons (page not loaded, element not found). Params: action (required — one of: navigate, navigate_provider, dom_query, dom_mutate, dom_pick, driver_exec, cookies_save, cookies_restore, screenshot, get_url, get_title, toast, click, type, scroll, hover, wait, wait_for, eval, zoom, find_in_page, stop_find_in_page, print, back, forward, reload, cookies_get, cookies_set, cookies_clear, storage_get, storage_set, network_block, network_intercept, picker_enable, picker_disable, inject, record_start, record_stop, url_listen, url_unlisten), data (object — action-specific: navigate needs {url}, screenshot needs {} (optional {rect} to capture a specific region), get_url/get_title need {}, toast needs {msg, type?(\"info\"|\"error\"|\"success\"|\"warn\"), durationMs?}, dom_query needs {selector}, dom_mutate needs {selector, value}, cookies_save/restore need {agentId}, url_listen needs {pattern, hook, agentId?, intercept?, capture?, label?}, url_unlisten needs {listenerId}).",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241717,
        "_key": "browser_action"
      },
      {
        "id": "agent_mesh_route",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
        "provides": "Spawn, message, route to, or queue work for a real ClearGlass agent-mesh node (clear-glass/src/mesh/agent-mesh.js) — a real, separate orchestration layer from a single provider chat (agent_chat) or a browser action (browser_action). \"route\" is RAID-governed pick-the-best-agent for a prompt; \"send\" addresses one already-spawned mesh node directly; \"enqueue\" adds to the real retry/escalation task queue instead of waiting synchronously. workflow_* actions reach the same mesh object's own real automation engine (the same one BrainOS's UI edits) — a real multi-step DSL (trigger/condition/agent/delay/command/branch/http/notification), not a separate system. Params: action (required — one of: spawn, send, route, enqueue, workflow_list, workflow_get, workflow_create, workflow_update, workflow_remove, workflow_run, workflow_step_add, workflow_step_update, workflow_step_remove, workflow_step_move, list_nodes, list_mesh_view, list_agents), data (object — action-specific: spawn needs {agentKey}, send needs {agentKey, prompt}, route needs {prompt}, enqueue needs a real task object, workflow_get/update/remove/run need {id}, workflow_create needs {name, ...}, workflow_step_* need {id, stepId, ...}, list_nodes/list_mesh_view/list_agents need {}. Every action here has a real, confirmed gate in clear-glass/src/gates/index.js — none of AgentMesh's real surface is unreachable now.",
        "updatedAt": 1789861241717,
        "_key": "agent_mesh_route"
      },
      {
        "id": "bookmarks_manage",
        "consumers": [],
        "intents": [],
        "edgeCases": [],
        "calls": 0,
        "file": null,
        "dir": null,
